# Tin · Sn · gate 50

**Tin** (Sn) is element **50** of the periodic table — a **post-transition metal**, period 5, group 14, p-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **118.71**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
Symbol Sn, from stannum; bronze with copper, solder for circuits; bends with a 'cry'; the humble can.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **50** falls on **0:1 — second valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **1**. That state is *the second reach — the diffuse, the airy, the not-quite-held* — the nature of emergence here is **ethereal**. Tin is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — ethereal
This emergent carries the **ethereal** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#9a7cff`.

